[00:00.36] There's no point standing around
[00:02.18] You'll only be showered by more boulders
[00:04.96] Ready your horses on the double
[00:07.75] Be honest, are all of us riding to our death?
[00:13.73] Yes, we are
[00:15.44] And since we're dying anyway, you're saying that it's better?
[00:19.81] Before we even start fighting?
[00:22.28] I am
[00:23.94] But wait, if we'll die anyway, then who cares what we do?
[00:28.79] We could just disobey your orders
[00:31.03] And it wouldn't mean a thing, would it?
[00:33.38] Yes, you're precisely right
[00:36.21] Everything that you thought had meaning
[00:38.26] Every hope, dream or moment of happiness
[00:41.65] None of it matters as you lie bleeding out on the battlefield
[00:45.86] None of it changes what a speeding rock does to a body
[00:49.02] We all die, but does that mean our lives are meaningless?
[00:55.45] Does that mean that there was no point being born?
[00:59.93] Would you say that about slain comrades?
[01:02.82] What about their lives?
[01:05.04] Were they meaningless?
[01:08.10] They were not
[01:09.81] Their memory serves as an example to us all
[01:13.31] The courageous fallen, the anguished fallen
[01:16.42] Their lives have meaning because
[01:18.13] We the living, refused to forget them
[01:20.79] And as we ride to certain death
[01:22.88] We trust our successors to do the same for us
[01:26.27] Because my soldiers do not fumble
[01:28.25] Or yield when faced with the cruelty of this world
[01:32.30] My soldiers push forward
[01:34.63] My soldiers scream out
[01:36.94] My soldiers rage
[01:39.86] 